  m_Name: 2_HostRange
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  ImageLeft: {fileID: 0}
  Title: 'Host Range: Natural Host(s):'
  Description: 'Humans, various monkey species, chimpanzees, gorillas, baboons, and
    duikers are natural animal hosts for ebolavirus. Serological evidence of immunity
    markers to ebolavirus in serum collected from domesticated dogs suggests asymptomatic
    infection is plausible, likely following exposure to infected humans or animal
    carrion. The Ebolavirus genome was discovered in two species of rodents and one
    species of shrew living in forest border areas, raising the possibility that these
    animals may be intermediary hosts. '
  ImageRight: {fileID: 0}
